# TypeScript conventions (Google TS style guide)

Follow https://google.github.io/styleguide/tsguide.html; Prettier (`gts`, `.prettierrc.json`) owns formatting via `npm run format`.

- `interface` for object shapes; `type` only for unions, `Record`s, tuples.
- Top-level functions are `function` declarations. One variable per declaration; no nested ternaries.
- Descriptive names; single letters only in scopes of 10 lines or fewer.
- No `as` or `!` without a runtime check; parsed JSON is `unknown` until a type guard validates it (`parseSpec(readJson(file))`, never `JSON.parse(text) as Spec`).
- JSDoc on non-obvious exports, `@fileoverview` per file, no types in JSDoc.
- Named exports only; `.ts` in relative imports; `node:` builtins.
- Errors: `throw new Error('<field|rule>: <reason>')`; CLIs wrap `main` in `run()` (prints `error: <message>`, exit 1).
- No new runtime dependencies; mark shortcuts with `ponytail:` naming the ceiling and upgrade path.

# Extending

- Field type: one `FIELD_TYPES` entry in `src/spec.ts` (`minKey`/`maxKey`/`floor`/`toValue`/`toPoint`, `defaultInvalid`); BVA, EP, pairwise and rules need no change.
- Formula function: one `FUNCTIONS` entry in `src/formula.ts`.
- Technique: `src/<technique>.ts` returning a `Result` with its own `import.meta.main` CLI (like `src/bva.ts`), plus a `TOOLS` entry in `src/mcp.ts`.
- Each new behaviour: one assertion in `src/check.ts` and the skill's spec docs updated in the same change.
